     bbaasseennaammee strips _f_i_l_e of any leading directory prefix
     (everything up to and including the last /). If the optional
     _s_u_f_f_i_x argument is given and the result ends with it,
     bbaasseennaammee strips that too.  bbaasseennaammee prints the result on the
     standard output.

     For example, the command

                  basename /usr/fred/source.c

     prints

                  source.c

     and the command

                  basename /usr/fred/source.c .c

     prints

